            },
            "style": "min-height: 70px",
            "text": "The MSI currently installs per-machine, which needs an administrator prompt. Most of our users' machines are single-user, and the WiX per-user mode avoids the prompt entirely. Upgrades still work in place.\n\nWhat changes: the install goes to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs instead of Program Files. Shortcuts are per-user. A machine-wide install stays available with an MSIINSTALLPERUSER=0 property for lab machines.\n\nI tested both modes on the Windows 11 VM: clean install, upgrade from 0.3, and uninstall. Both passed. The per-user build is 2 MB smaller because it skips the service registration we don't use.",
            "textColor": "#000000d8",
            "width": 308,
